From: Highball engine proposal contributors
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] ntdll: AoE IV Rosetta softfault bridge and immutable code cache

Recovered GameToMac 0.1.5-alpha Wine changes by Marc Ibrahim (LGPL-2.1+),
via NerRobDog/wine-aoe4 at 711c6fc7559a565c417aab4d52d84b09767a9c1d.
Includes NerRobDog's near-Jcc relocation extension and cache diagnostics.
HDE notices are preserved. The matching softfault-capable x87sidecar is
required; generic i386 cooperative attach does not supply this hook.

Adapted to Highball's pinned CrossOver 26.3 base plus patches 0001-0016.
Reuses 0012's cooperative protocol, deferring only the AoE attach until
ntdll and the bridge are mapped. Checks the SHA256 of the same descriptor
Wine uses for SEC_IMAGE, plus the mapped x64 image base, before attaching
or enabling the cache. Opt-in only, default engines are unchanged.

Verification: Linux portable guard/relocator/cache tests and patch
application against the pinned source plus Highball's existing series.
No macOS build, Rosetta or game verification yet. Game build pinned to
5380c577805565817f528af6eac385263413fa6815553f9a31fa62561cb45e8c.
Upstream status: proposal only; no issue or PR filed.

